{% doc %}
  Renders all meta tags for the page including Open Graph, Twitter Cards, and SEO tags.

  @param {object} [product] - The product object, available on product pages for price meta tags.
{% enddoc %}

<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta
  http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible"
  content="IE=edge"
>
<meta
  name="viewport"
  content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"
>
<meta
  name="theme-color"
  content=""
>

{%- liquid
  comment
    Sultan of Statues: shop.name, the store SEO title and the store
    description are store-level and still say "Mum Where's My Cards". The
    theme substitutes its own brand name so staging never shows the old
    card-shop identity. Remove this once the store itself is renamed.
  endcomment
  assign sos_brand = settings.sos_brand_name | default: shop.name

  assign og_title = page_title | default: shop.name
  assign og_title = og_title | replace: shop.name, sos_brand
  if request.page_type == 'index' and settings.sos_home_title != blank
    assign og_title = settings.sos_home_title
  endif

  comment
    Sultan of Statues: buyers search "one piece statues", "gear 5 luffy
    statue", "one piece resin statues" — the words "statue" and "resin"
    carry the buying intent and were missing from every product title.
    Built here rather than typed into six admin SEO fields so the rule
    holds for anything added later.

    The studio ALWAYS stays in. An earlier version dropped it to hold the
    title under 60 characters and that was the wrong trade: "jimei palace"
    is precisely what a collector types, and there is no 60-character
    ranking rule — Google truncates on pixel width per device. Losing the
    studio to save eight characters cost the best term on the page.

    Scale is appended only where the product type records it, so nothing
    is claimed about pieces that have not been measured. The shop name is
    not appended below, because Google prints the site name beside the URL
    anyway.
  endcomment
  assign sos_own_title = false
  assign sos_own_description = false
  assign sos_share_asset = ''
  if request.page_type == 'product' and product != blank
    assign sos_t = product.title
    if product.type contains '1/6'
      assign sos_t = sos_t | append: ' 1/6'
    endif
    assign sos_t = sos_t | append: ' Resin Statue'
    if product.vendor != blank
      assign sos_t = sos_t | append: ' – ' | append: product.vendor
    endif
    if product.tags contains 'One Piece'
      assign sos_t = sos_t | append: ' | One Piece UK'
    else
      assign sos_t = sos_t | append: ' | UK'
    endif
    assign og_title = sos_t
    assign sos_own_title = true

    comment
      Factual product description: studio, scale, franchise, condition,
      location. No adjectives — Google matches on the attributes a collector
      types, and the superlatives a shop reaches for match nothing.
    endcomment
    capture sos_d
      echo 'Pre-owned '
      if product.vendor != blank
        echo product.vendor
        echo ' '
      endif
      echo product.title
      if product.type contains '1/6'
        echo ' 1/6'
      endif
      echo ' resin statue. UK stock, original box, photographs of the exact piece, inspected condition and personal UK delivery or free London collection.'
    endcapture
    assign sos_own_description = true
  endif

  comment
    Episode 001. The Shopify article title is the story title, which is not
    what a buyer searches; the H1 and the search title are the question they
    actually type. Set here so the article keeps its story title in admin
    and in the blog index while still carrying a search-shaped title tag.
    Title 56 characters, description 153.
  endcomment
  if request.page_type == 'article' and article.handle == 'the-statue-that-looked-perfect'
    assign og_title = '7 Things to Check Before Buying a Pre-Owned Resin Statue'
    assign sos_own_title = true
    capture sos_d
      echo 'Studio, actual-item photos, damage, parts, packaging, delivery and total cost — the seven checks before buying a pre-owned resin statue, told as a manga.'
    endcapture
    assign sos_own_description = true

    comment
      Share card. The scenes themselves are portrait (1122x1402) and crop
      badly to the 1.91:1 that Facebook, LinkedIn and X all want, so this
      is a landscape crop of scene one — the same artwork, nothing added.
      Used only when the article has no featured image of its own, so
      setting one in admin still wins.
    endcomment
    assign sos_share_asset = 'collectors-journey-ep001-share.jpg'
  endif

  if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection.handle == 'one-piece-statues'
    comment
      Approved copy. The title carries the brand, so the shop-name suffix
      below is suppressed to avoid printing it twice. 58 characters.
    endcomment
    assign og_title = 'One Piece Resin Statues UK | Pre-Owned | Sultan of Statues'
    assign sos_own_title = true

    comment
      The inherited description described the delivery service, which is
      what the page does AFTER the sale, not what it contains. A category
      snippet has to answer "is what I searched for in here".

      Fixed text, not generated. An earlier version interpolated
      collection.all_vendors, which ran to 240 characters and listed both
      "Jimei Palace" and "Anikingdom x Jimei Palace" as separate studios.

      Approved copy at 159 characters, tightened to 154 by dropping the
      word "Shop" — Google truncates around 155 on desktop and shorter on
      mobile, and the resale hook at the end is the part worth keeping.
    endcomment
    capture sos_d
      echo 'Your statue deserves more than a shipping label. Pre-owned One Piece resin statues with personal delivery, optional setup, box storage and resale support.'
    endcapture
    assign sos_own_description = true
  endif

  assign og_url = canonical_url | default: request.origin
  assign og_type = 'website'
  assign og_description = page_description | default: shop.description | default: shop.name
  assign og_description = og_description | replace: shop.name, sos_brand
  if request.page_type == 'index' and settings.sos_meta_description != blank
    assign og_description = settings.sos_meta_description
  endif
  if sos_own_description
    assign og_description = sos_d
  endif

  if request.page_type == 'product'
    assign og_type = 'product'
  elsif request.page_type == 'article'
    assign og_type = 'article'
  elsif request.page_type == 'password'
    assign og_url = request.origin
  endif

  comment
    Site name for Google's site-name feature. Google reads og:site_name and
    WebSite.name among other signals, and asks that they agree with each
    other; it chooses what to display and may take time, or keep showing
    the domain. These are the signals, not a switch.
  endcomment
  assign sos_site_name = settings.sos_site_name | default: sos_brand
%}

<meta
  property="og:site_name"
  content="{{ sos_site_name }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:url"
  content="{{ og_url }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:title"
  content="{{ og_title | escape }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:type"
  content="{{ og_type }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:description"
  content="{{ og_description | escape }}"
>

{%- if page_image -%}
  <meta
    property="og:image"
    content="http:{{ page_image | image_url }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:secure_url"
    content="https:{{ page_image | image_url }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:width"
    content="{{ page_image.width }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:height"
    content="{{ page_image.height }}"
  >
{%- elsif sos_share_asset != blank -%}
  {%- assign sos_card = sos_share_asset | asset_url -%}
  <meta
    property="og:image"
    content="{{ sos_card }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:secure_url"
    content="{{ sos_card }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:width"
    content="1200"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:height"
    content="630"
  >
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Sultan of Statues: the homepage and the policy pages carry no page_image,
    so a share of them rendered as a blank card. The palace hero stands in —
    it is already a derivative in the theme, so this costs no extra weight.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign sos_share = 'sos-hero-palace-desktop-1774.jpg' | asset_url -%}
  <meta
    property="og:image"
    content="{{ sos_share }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:secure_url"
    content="{{ sos_share }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:width"
    content="1774"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:height"
    content="683"
  >
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  <meta
    property="og:price:amount"
    content="{{ product.price | money_without_currency | strip_html }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:price:currency"
    content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}"
  >
{%- endif -%}

{%- if settings.social_twitter_link != blank -%}
  <meta
    name="twitter:site"
    content="{{ settings.social_twitter_link | split: 'twitter.com/' | last | prepend: '@' }}"
  >
{%- endif -%}
<meta
  name="twitter:card"
  content="summary_large_image"
>
<meta
  name="twitter:title"
  content="{{ og_title | escape }}"
>
<meta
  name="twitter:description"
  content="{{ og_description | escape }}"
>

<title>
  {{ og_title }}
  {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; tagged "{{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}"{% endif -%}
  {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
  {%- unless sos_own_title or og_title contains sos_brand %} &ndash; {{ sos_brand }}{% endunless -%}
</title>

{%- liquid
  comment
    Sultan of Statues: /collections/all serves the same six pieces and the
    same copy as /collections/one-piece-statues, so left alone the two split
    the ranking signal for the term the shop is actually chasing. The
    catch-all points at the named collection instead.
  endcomment
  assign sos_canonical = canonical_url
  if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection.handle == 'all'
    assign sos_canonical = shop.url | append: routes.collections_url | append: '/one-piece-statues'
  endif
-%}
<link
  rel="canonical"
  href="{{ sos_canonical }}"
>

{% if og_description != blank %}
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="{{ og_description | escape }}"
  >
{% endif %}

{%- comment -%}
  Homepage only: WebSite structured data, which is one of the signals
  Google reads for the site name shown beside a result. Emitted on the
  index alone because Google takes the site name from the homepage, and a
  second WebSite node on inner pages would add nothing and risk conflict.

  No SearchAction is declared: the sitelinks search box it used to drive
  was retired, and claiming a feature we do not implement is noise.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "name": {{ sos_site_name | json }},
      "url": {{ request.origin | append: routes.root_url | json }}
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
